# Manual requests against the AG-UI endpoint (JetBrains HTTP Client).
# Start the server first: `npm run start:agent`. The server binds to loopback
# (127.0.0.1:3001) and validates every body against RunAgentInputSchema.
#
# A dummy API key is enough to explore the transport: the run then terminates
# with a RUN_ERROR event naming the provider failure. Real answers need a real
# key in `.env`.

### Valid run — streams AG-UI events as SSE (RUN_STARTED … RUN_FINISHED/RUN_ERROR)
POST http://localhost:3001/ag-ui/assistant
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: text/event-stream

{
  "threadId": "http-client-thread",
  "runId": "http-client-run-1",
  "messages": [
    { "id": "m1", "role": "user", "content": "Which Angular conferences are there?" }
  ],
  "tools": [],
  "context": [],
  "state": {}
}

### Invalid body — 400 with the zod issues
POST http://localhost:3001/ag-ui/assistant
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "threadId": "only-this"
}

### Unknown agent id — 404
POST http://localhost:3001/ag-ui/does-not-exist
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "threadId": "http-client-thread",
  "runId": "http-client-run-2",
  "messages": [],
  "tools": [],
  "context": [],
  "state": {}
}

### CORS preflight — 204, allow-origin echoes the shell origin
OPTIONS http://localhost:3001/ag-ui/assistant
Origin: http://localhost:4200
Access-Control-Request-Method: POST
